/terraform/.terraform
# Per-environment local overrides: the ACS connection string, the captcha secret, the alert
# address, a workstation's own IP for the Key Vault firewall. tf.sh passes the one matching the
# environment you asked for. Every environment, not just dev - the old single-environment line here
# meant doing MAIL-02 the documented way for prod staged prod's ACS connection string and captcha
# secret for commit.
terraform/*.local.tfvars
# The name these used to have. Terraform auto-loads any *.auto.tfvars on every run whatever
# -var-file is passed, so one of these leaks its values into every other environment's plan; tf.sh
# refuses to run while one exists. Still ignored so that a leftover cannot be committed either.
terraform/*.local.auto.tfvars
# A saved plan holds the resource values it would write, secrets among them, in the clear - and
# `plan -out=` is the workflow tf.sh's own header documents, so the file lands here by following
# the instructions rather than by going off them. Exactly TF-07's shape: the remedy the docs
# prescribe is what stages the secret.
terraform/*.tfplan
terraform/errored.tfstate
